sed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-01T11:36:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T02:37:13Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116924","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116924","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116924.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116924.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Bugfix: Fix Tree popup editor floating/misplacing after window move or resize\r\n\r\nFixes the inline cell editor popup (used for node renaming and editable Tree cells) appearing at a wrong screen position or drifting after the editor window is moved or resized. on tiling window managers (Awesome, i3, Sway) the popup appears as an\r\nuntitled OS window at a random screen corner instead of over the target cell. On all platforms, the popup freezes at its original screen coordinates when the editor window is dragged or resized, and only disappears when Escape or Enter is pressed.\r\n\r\nThe problem was never in how the editor initiates the rename — it was in how Tree itself repositions the popup on transform change.\r\n\r\nFixes #116875\r\n\r\n##  Changes\r\n\r\n**`scene/gui/tree.cpp` — `NOTIFICATION_TRANSFORM_CHANGED` handler**\r\n\r\nThe handler that repositions the popup when the `Tree`'s transform changes (window move, resize, scroll) was calling:\r\n```cpp\r\n// Before — broken\r\npopup_editor->set_position(get_global_position() + rect.position);\r\npopup_editor->set_size(rect.size);\r\n```","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116924/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116924/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}